    "headline": "India eases rules for rupee export payments, seeks to widen trade settlement",
    "body": "India has eased export payment rules, allowing rupee settlements with non-Asian Clearing Union countries. This move aims to promote wider use of the local currency in international trade transactions. Eligible rupee export receipts will now qualify for trade-policy benefits and count towards exporter obligations. The changes align with recent Reserve Bank of India foreign-exchange rules permitting broader rupee usage.",
